> In this model, lambda is the expected number of individuals in year 1.
> Abundance after year 1 is modeled as the sum of 2 random variables
> (recruits and survivors). So if you want to model abundance throughout
> time, you need to model lambda as a function of corn in year 1, and gamma
> and/or omega as a function of corn. In other words, in addition to
> supplying corn as a yearlySiteCov, you need to create a siteCov that has
> the corn data from the first year:
