Hi Andy -

I estimated the dispersion parameter to be 1.3 and used that along with the MuMIn package to compute QAICc and as you suspect it doesn't really impact the value of the parameter estimates much at all.

Using GLM estimates as starting values did not change the final converged values of the parameters either.

Can you be more specific in what you mean by 'organization of the data'?  I've reduced collinearity to acceptable levels by identifying problematic covariates using condition numbers and
variance decomposition proportions (Belsley, Kuh, and Welsch (1980)) as implemented in the 'perturb' package in R.  I have also mean centered and scaled all variables.  What other 'data organization' considerations exist?

Thanks for you help
Patrick

